## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates the ability to design tenant-isolated logging architecture using Cloud Logging sinks, IAM least privilege principles, CMEK encryption, and automated validation in a shared GCP project multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant log sinks with resource and label-based filtering
- Least-privilege IAM roles for secure log export operations
- Customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK) for log data protection
- Log-based monitoring and alerting for leakage detection
- CI/CD automated validation using synthetic tenant provisioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate tenant log isolation in CI pipeline
const tenantId = process.env.TENANT_ID;
const logs = readLogs({
  filter: `resource.labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  timeRange: '1h'
});

// Verify no cross-tenant log contamination
const crossTenantLeaks = logs.filter(log => 
  log.labels.tenant_id !== tenantId
);

if (crossTenantLeaks.length > 0) {
  throw new Error('Tenant log isolation violation detected');
}
```

